    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d713">

                <pb facs="0931" n="921" xml:id="pg921"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.248/11–1747</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Chinese Minister</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Tan</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the
                        Chief of the Division of Chinese Affairs</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Ringwalt</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1947-11-17">November 17,
                        1947</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Dear Mr. Ringwalt</hi>: As you are aware, an
                    agreement has been signed in China regarding certain items of equipment and
                    material under the 8⅓ Group Program for the Chinese Air Force by representatives
                    of our two governments. I am directed by the Ambassador to express to you that
                    my government would appreciate it very much if instructions could be sent to the
                    United States representatives in China and the Pacific Zone to expedite delivery
                    of such items and material.</p>
                <p>Yours sincerely,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Shao-Hwa Tan</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
